"1. Personnel Security"@en owl:sameAs "1. Personnel Security"@en .

"2. Asset Management"@en owl:sameAs "2. Asset Management"@en .

"3. Physical and Environmental Security"@en owl:sameAs "3. Physical and Environmental Security"@en .

"4. Access Control"@en owl:sameAs "4. Access Control"@en .

"5. ICT Security Requirements"@en owl:sameAs "5. ICT Security Requirements"@en .

"6. Communications Security"@en owl:sameAs "6. Communications Security"@en .

"7. Classified Information Management"@en owl:sameAs "7. Classified Information Management"@en .

"8. Incidents and Compromise"@en owl:sameAs "8. Incidents and Compromise"@en .

"A 'shall' requirement from a normative standard (ISO, NEN)."@en owl:sameAs "A 'shall' requirement from a normative standard (ISO, NEN)."@en .

"A Category from NIST Cybersecurity Framework 2.0. Categories are subdivisions of Functions that group related cybersecurity outcomes. CSF 2.0 has 22 Categories distributed across 6 Functions."@en owl:sameAs "A Category from NIST Cybersecurity Framework 2.0. Categories are subdivisions of Functions that group related cybersecurity outcomes. CSF 2.0 has 22 Categories distributed across 6 Functions."@en .

"A Function from NIST Cybersecurity Framework 2.0. Functions form the highest level of the CSF Core: GOVERN, IDENTIFY, PROTECT, DETECT, RESPOND, RECOVER. Per CSF 2.0 GOVERN is new compared to v1.x."@en owl:sameAs "A Function from NIST Cybersecurity Framework 2.0. Functions form the highest level of the CSF Core: GOVERN, IDENTIFY, PROTECT, DETECT, RESPOND, RECOVER. Per CSF 2.0 GOVERN is new compared to v1.x."@en .

"A Subcategory from NIST Cybersecurity Framework 2.0. Subcategories describe specific technical and management outcomes that realise a Category. CSF 2.0 has 106 Subcategories with format XX.YY-NN (e.g. GV.OC-01)."@en owl:sameAs "A Subcategory from NIST Cybersecurity Framework 2.0. Subcategories describe specific technical and management outcomes that realise a Category. CSF 2.0 has 106 Subcategories with format XX.YY-NN (e.g. GV.OC-01)."@en .

"A business service whose disruption would have significant impact on public tasks, safety or trust. Relevant for NIS2 Art.21(c) and ISO 22301 scoping."@en owl:sameAs "A business service whose disruption would have significant impact on public tasks, safety or trust. Relevant for NIS2 Art.21(c) and ISO 22301 scoping."@en .

"A classification level for bijzondere informatie as defined in VIRBI 2025 art. 4. Four levels: Dep.V, Stg.C, Stg.G, Stg.ZG."@en owl:sameAs "A classification level for bijzondere informatie as defined in VIRBI 2025 art. 4. Four levels: Dep.V, Stg.C, Stg.G, Stg.ZG."@en .

"A compliance requirement is satisfied by one or more controls."@en owl:sameAs "A compliance requirement is satisfied by one or more controls."@en .

"A component of the COSO Internal Control or Enterprise Risk Management framework."@en owl:sameAs "A component of the COSO Internal Control or Enterprise Risk Management framework."@en .

"A composite asset consisting of data collections, procedures, processes, software and facilities for storage, processing and communication. Per Besluit CIO-stelsel Rijksdienst 2026 art. 1o. Components are linked via asset:hasComponent. Persons who operate the system are linked via asset:isOperatedBy — NOT via asset:hasComponent (masterchat decision D-M18-5: CIO-stelsel primary source, not VIRBI 2025 / VIR 2007 which do include 'personen' in the informatiesysteem definition)."@en owl:sameAs "A composite asset consisting of data collections, procedures, processes, software and facilities for storage, processing and communication. Per Besluit CIO-stelsel Rijksdienst 2026 art. 1o. Components are linked via asset:hasComponent. Persons who operate the system are linked via asset:isOperatedBy — NOT via asset:hasComponent (masterchat decision D-M18-5: CIO-stelsel primary source, not VIRBI 2025 / VIR 2007 which do include 'personen' in the informatiesysteem definition)."@en .

"A constituent part of an asset. Used as range (together with asset:Asset) for mereological relations (asset:hasComponent) and for control-applicability (asset:appliesToAssetType). Components are typed per asset subclass — see CIO-stelsel art. 1o for the canonical InformationSystem components."@en owl:sameAs "A constituent part of an asset. Used as range (together with asset:Asset) for mereological relations (asset:hasComponent) and for control-applicability (asset:appliesToAssetType). Components are typed per asset subclass — see CIO-stelsel art. 1o for the canonical InformationSystem components."@en .

"A control defined in ISO/IEC 27002:2022, organised in four themes: Organisational, People, Physical, Technological."@en owl:sameAs "A control defined in ISO/IEC 27002:2022, organised in four themes: Organisational, People, Physical, Technological."@en .

"A cybersecurity supply chain risk management program, strategy, objectives, policies, and processes are established and agreed to by organizational stakeholders"@en owl:sameAs "A cybersecurity supply chain risk management program, strategy, objectives, policies, and processes are established and agreed to by organizational stakeholders"@en .

"A defined level in a capability maturity model. Based on COBIT 2019 / CMMI scale (0–5)."@en owl:sameAs "A defined level in a capability maturity model. Based on COBIT 2019 / CMMI scale (0–5)."@en .

"A defined, repeatable activity that contributes to the operation of the ISMS."@en owl:sameAs "A defined, repeatable activity that contributes to the operation of the ISMS."@en .

"A department, team, directorate or other formal organisational grouping."@en owl:sameAs "A department, team, directorate or other formal organisational grouping."@en .

"A described sequence of events that may result in the materialisation of a risk, including the threat, the exploited vulnerability and the impact on one or more assets."@en owl:sameAs "A described sequence of events that may result in the materialisation of a risk, including the threat, the exploited vulnerability and the impact on one or more assets."@en .

"A document required by ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Clause 6.1.3(d) listing all Annex A controls with applicability decisions, implementation status and justifications."@en owl:sameAs "A document required by ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Clause 6.1.3(d) listing all Annex A controls with applicability decisions, implementation status and justifications."@en .

"A documented plan describing corrective actions, owners, timelines and success criteria."@en owl:sameAs "A documented plan describing corrective actions, owners, timelines and success criteria."@en .

"A documented record of identified risks, their assessment results, treatment decisions and residual risk."@en owl:sameAs "A documented record of identified risks, their assessment results, treatment decisions and residual risk."@en .

"A domain in which impact may be experienced: financial, operational, reputational, legal, safety."@en owl:sameAs "A domain in which impact may be experienced: financial, operational, reputational, legal, safety."@en .

"A domain-specific area covered by the ENSIA audit framework. Each domain has its own toezichthouder (supervisory authority) and specific norms."@en owl:sameAs "A domain-specific area covered by the ENSIA audit framework. Each domain has its own toezichthouder (supervisory authority) and specific norms."@en .

"A duty assigned to a role to perform or oversee a specific GRC activity."@en owl:sameAs "A duty assigned to a role to perform or oversee a specific GRC activity."@en .

"A duty imposed on the organisation by a legal instrument, regulation, standard or contract."@en owl:sameAs "A duty imposed on the organisation by a legal instrument, regulation, standard or contract."@en .

"A facility that supports an information system: storage, processing or communication. Per CIO-stelsel 2026 art. 1o 'voorzieningen voor opslag, verwerking en communicatie'. Subclassed into StorageFacility, ProcessingFacility and CommunicationFacility."@en owl:sameAs "A facility that supports an information system: storage, processing or communication. Per CIO-stelsel 2026 art. 1o 'voorzieningen voor opslag, verwerking en communicatie'. Subclassed into StorageFacility, ProcessingFacility and CommunicationFacility."@en .

"A finding that is not a nonconformity but indicates a potential improvement area."@en owl:sameAs "A finding that is not a nonconformity but indicates a potential improvement area."@en .

"A formal document expressing the organisation's risk appetite, approved by senior management. [NIST SP 800-39 / ISO 31000]"@en owl:sameAs "A formal document expressing the organisation's risk appetite, approved by senior management. [NIST SP 800-39 / ISO 31000]"@en .

"A formal evaluation of the current maturity level of a GRC domain or control area."@en owl:sameAs "A formal evaluation of the current maturity level of a GRC domain or control area."@en .

"A framework for the governance and management of enterprise IT, published by ISACA."@en owl:sameAs "A framework for the governance and management of enterprise IT, published by ISACA."@en .

"A framework or methodology representing industry-accepted good practice, not formally standardised."@en owl:sameAs "A framework or methodology representing industry-accepted good practice, not formally standardised."@en .

"A high-level management direction document. Mandatory for ISO 27001:2022 Clause 5.2."@en owl:sameAs "A high-level management direction document. Mandatory for ISO 27001:2022 Clause 5.2."@en .

"A high-level organisational objective derived from the mission and strategy. GRC activities are aligned to support these objectives. [COBIT 2019 / ISO 31000:2018 §6.2]"@en owl:sameAs "A high-level organisational objective derived from the mission and strategy. GRC activities are aligned to support these objectives. [COBIT 2019 / ISO 31000:2018 §6.2]"@en .

"A law, decree or policy instrument issued by the Dutch national government."@en owl:sameAs "A law, decree or policy instrument issued by the Dutch national government."@en .

"A legally binding instrument issued by a governmental or supranational authority."@en owl:sameAs "A legally binding instrument issued by a governmental or supranational authority."@en .

"A mandatory minimum security baseline mandated for a government sector."@en owl:sameAs "A mandatory minimum security baseline mandated for a government sector."@en .

"A measurable value that demonstrates how effectively a GRC objective is being achieved. [COBIT 2019 / ISO 27004]"@en owl:sameAs "A measurable value that demonstrates how effectively a GRC objective is being achieved. [COBIT 2019 / ISO 27004]"@en .

"A metric indicating the effectiveness of a specific control. [COBIT 2019]"@en owl:sameAs "A metric indicating the effectiveness of a specific control. [COBIT 2019]"@en .

"A metric used to indicate the likelihood that a risk will exceed the organisation's risk tolerance threshold. [COBIT 2019 / ISO 31000]"@en owl:sameAs "A metric used to indicate the likelihood that a risk will exceed the organisation's risk tolerance threshold. [COBIT 2019 / ISO 31000]"@en .

"A ministerial decision under Cbb art. 18 that obliges an essential or important entity not to use products or services from specified parties in designated network and information systems, where necessary to manage national security risks. ABox population is Spoor B (dependent on actual ministerial decisions)."@en owl:sameAs "A ministerial decision under Cbb art. 18 that obliges an essential or important entity not to use products or services from specified parties in designated network and information systems, where necessary to manage national security risks. ABox population is Spoor B (dependent on actual ministerial decisions)."@en .

"A named confidentiality level applied to information assets. Aligned with VIR 2007 and VIRBI 2025 classification scheme."@en owl:sameAs "A named confidentiality level applied to information assets. Aligned with VIR 2007 and VIRBI 2025 classification scheme."@en .

"A non-binding document providing guidance on implementation of controls or requirements."@en owl:sameAs "A non-binding document providing guidance on implementation of controls or requirements."@en .

"A nonconformity that affects the capability of the ISMS to achieve intended results or violates a legal obligation."@en owl:sameAs "A nonconformity that affects the capability of the ISMS to achieve intended results or violates a legal obligation."@en .

"A normative document published by a recognised standards body (e.g. ISO, NEN, NIST)."@en owl:sameAs "A normative document published by a recognised standards body (e.g. ISO, NEN, NIST)."@en .

"A person creates their own estimates of impact and scope"@en owl:sameAs "A person creates their own estimates of impact and scope"@en .

"A person or entity with the accountability and authority to manage a risk."@en owl:sameAs "A person or entity with the accountability and authority to manage a risk."@en .

"A potential cause of an unwanted incident that may result in harm to a system or organisation. [ISO/IEC 27000:2018]"@en owl:sameAs "A potential cause of an unwanted incident that may result in harm to a system or organisation. [ISO/IEC 27000:2018]"@en .

"A process executing within an information system. Per CIO-stelsel 2026 art. 1o 'proces'. Naming 'SystemProcess' (not 'Process') to avoid ambiguity with business-processes (biz:) or risk-processes (risk:)."@en owl:sameAs "A process executing within an information system. Per CIO-stelsel 2026 art. 1o 'proces'. Naming 'SystemProcess' (not 'Process') to avoid ambiguity with business-processes (biz:) or risk-processes (risk:)."@en .

"A process to modify risk. Treatment options: modify (mitigate), retain (accept), avoid, share/transfer. [ISO 31000:2018]"@en owl:sameAs "A process to modify risk. Treatment options: modify (mitigate), retain (accept), avoid, share/transfer. [ISO 31000:2018]"@en .

"A qualitative level of impact on a defined scale."@en owl:sameAs "A qualitative level of impact on a defined scale."@en .

"A qualitative level of likelihood on a defined scale."@en owl:sameAs "A qualitative level of likelihood on a defined scale."@en .

"A reified assignment linking a Role to a GRCActivity with a specific RACI type (R/A/C/I)."@en owl:sameAs "A reified assignment linking a Role to a GRCActivity with a specific RACI type (R/A/C/I)."@en .

"A repeatable set of activities that delivers a defined business output or service."@en owl:sameAs "A repeatable set of activities that delivers a defined business output or service."@en .

"A result of evaluating collected audit evidence against audit criteria."@en owl:sameAs "A result of evaluating collected audit evidence against audit criteria."@en .

"A risk has potential consequences for one or more assets."@en owl:sameAs "A risk has potential consequences for one or more assets."@en .

"A risk specific to information security: the potential that a threat will exploit a vulnerability of an information asset causing harm to the organisation."@en owl:sameAs "A risk specific to information security: the potential that a threat will exploit a vulnerability of an information asset causing harm to the organisation."@en .

"A scheduled overview of recurring GRC obligations and activities (reporting deadlines, audits, reviews, training cycles)."@en owl:sameAs "A scheduled overview of recurring GRC obligations and activities (reporting deadlines, audits, reviews, training cycles)."@en .

"A security or privacy control defined in NIST SP 800-53 Revision 5."@en owl:sameAs "A security or privacy control defined in NIST SP 800-53 Revision 5."@en .

"A set of planned audits covering a defined scope and time period."@en owl:sameAs "A set of planned audits covering a defined scope and time period."@en .

