"Indicates that compliance with the subject framework substantially covers the requirements of the object framework. This is a directional, non-symmetric relationship: A fw:dektAf B means implementing A satisfies (most of) B's requirements."@en owl:sameAs "Indicates that compliance with the subject framework substantially covers the requirements of the object framework. This is a directional, non-symmetric relationship: A fw:dektAf B means implementing A satisfies (most of) B's requirements."@en .

"Indicates that the subject framework legally mandates the implementation of the object framework. E.g. VIR 2007 mandates BIO 2.0 for the Dutch central government."@en owl:sameAs "Indicates that the subject framework legally mandates the implementation of the object framework. E.g. VIR 2007 mandates BIO 2.0 for the Dutch central government."@en .

"Indicates that the subject framework provides the IT-specific implementation or operationalisation of the (broader, enterprise-level) object framework. E.g. COBIT fw:geeftITInvullingAan COSO ICF."@en owl:sameAs "Indicates that the subject framework provides the IT-specific implementation or operationalisation of the (broader, enterprise-level) object framework. E.g. COBIT fw:geeftITInvullingAan COSO ICF."@en .

"Indicates that the subject framework serves as an audit or assessment instrument for the object framework. E.g. ENSIA fw:toetst BIO 2.0."@en owl:sameAs "Indicates that the subject framework serves as an audit or assessment instrument for the object framework. E.g. ENSIA fw:toetst BIO 2.0."@en .

"Indicates that this framework version supersedes an earlier version."@en owl:sameAs "Indicates that this framework version supersedes an earlier version."@en .

"Indicates whether compliance with this framework is legally mandatory for Dutch government entities."@en owl:sameAs "Indicates whether compliance with this framework is legally mandatory for Dutch government entities."@en .

