"Relates a control to the asset type(s) — asset-class or component-class — for which it is relevant. Class-level property (Spoor A): the object is an asset-class, not an instance. Instance-level applicability (Spoor B) follows once the asset inventory is populated. Placed in asset:-namespace per masterchat-decision D-M18-2 (Option 2b) to respect the no-changes-to-M02 constraint (DEEL 7.3 of M18 chatstarter)."@en owl:sameAs "Relates a control to the asset type(s) — asset-class or component-class — for which it is relevant. Class-level property (Spoor A): the object is an asset-class, not an instance. Instance-level applicability (Spoor B) follows once the asset inventory is populated. Placed in asset:-namespace per masterchat-decision D-M18-2 (Option 2b) to respect the no-changes-to-M02 constraint (DEEL 7.3 of M18 chatstarter)."@en .

"Relates an information system to the persons who operate it. Distinct from asset:hasComponent (masterchat-decision D-M18-5, Option A): persons are not mereological parts of a system. Note: VIR 2007 art. 1b, VIRBI 2025 art. 1 and BIO 2.0 DO include 'personen' in their information-system definition; this model follows Besluit CIO-stelsel 2026 art. 1o as primary source for architectural cleanliness."@en owl:sameAs "Relates an information system to the persons who operate it. Distinct from asset:hasComponent (masterchat-decision D-M18-5, Option A): persons are not mereological parts of a system. Note: VIR 2007 art. 1b, VIRBI 2025 art. 1 and BIO 2.0 DO include 'personen' in their information-system definition; this model follows Besluit CIO-stelsel 2026 art. 1o as primary source for architectural cleanliness."@en .

