"The official publication date of the framework or its version."@en owl:sameAs "The official publication date of the framework or its version."@en .

"The official web location where the framework can be accessed."@en owl:sameAs "The official web location where the framework can be accessed."@en .

"The operational core statement of a control: a concise description of the measure to be taken or outcome to be achieved. Distinguished from rdfs:comment: rdfs:comment may contain explanatory context; ext:hasControlStatement is the normative core requirement. First use in v4.4.0: 26 ctrl:CBWControl individuals (sheet 3 column F Beheersmaatregel text). Generic domain ctrl:Control makes it reusable for future NIST CSF, NIST 800-53, ISO 27002 controls."@en owl:sameAs "The operational core statement of a control: a concise description of the measure to be taken or outcome to be achieved. Distinguished from rdfs:comment: rdfs:comment may contain explanatory context; ext:hasControlStatement is the normative core requirement. First use in v4.4.0: 26 ctrl:CBWControl individuals (sheet 3 column F Beheersmaatregel text). Generic domain ctrl:Control makes it reusable for future NIST CSF, NIST 800-53, ISO 27002 controls."@en .

"The organisation's primary ISMS, certified per ISO/IEC 27001:2022, also covering BIO 2.0 and NIS2/CBW obligations."@en owl:sameAs "The organisation's primary ISMS, certified per ISO/IEC 27001:2022, also covering BIO 2.0 and NIS2/CBW obligations."@en .

"The organization adapts its cybersecurity practices based on previous and current cybersecurity activities, including lessons learned and predictive indicators. Through a process of continuous improvement that incorporates advanced cybersecurity technologies and practices, the organization actively adapts to a changing technological landscape and responds in a timely and effective manner to evolving, sophisticated threats. The organization uses real-time or near real-time information to understand and consistently act upon the cybersecurity risks associated with its suppliers and the products and services it acquires and uses. Cybersecurity information is constantly shared throughout the organization and with authorized third parties."@en a xsd:string ;
    owl:sameAs "The organization adapts its cybersecurity practices based on previous and current cybersecurity activities, including lessons learned and predictive indicators. Through a process of continuous improvement that incorporates advanced cybersecurity technologies and practices, the organization actively adapts to a changing technological landscape and responds in a timely and effective manner to evolving, sophisticated threats. The organization uses real-time or near real-time information to understand and consistently act upon the cybersecurity risks associated with its suppliers and the products and services it acquires and uses. Cybersecurity information is constantly shared throughout the organization and with authorized third parties."@en .

"The organization's risk management practices are formally approved and expressed as policy. Risk-informed policies, processes, and procedures are defined, implemented as intended, and reviewed. Organizational cybersecurity practices are regularly updated based on the application of risk management processes to changes in business/mission requirements, threats, and technological landscape."@en a xsd:string ;
    owl:sameAs "The organization's risk management practices are formally approved and expressed as policy. Risk-informed policies, processes, and procedures are defined, implemented as intended, and reviewed. Organizational cybersecurity practices are regularly updated based on the application of risk management processes to changes in business/mission requirements, threats, and technological landscape."@en .

"The organizational mission is understood and informs cybersecurity risk management"@en owl:sameAs "The organizational mission is understood and informs cybersecurity risk management"@en .

"The organization’s current cybersecurity risks are understood"@en owl:sameAs "The organization’s current cybersecurity risks are understood"@en .

"The organization’s cybersecurity risk management strategy, expectations, and policy are established, communicated, and monitored"@en owl:sameAs "The organization’s cybersecurity risk management strategy, expectations, and policy are established, communicated, and monitored"@en .

"The organization’s personnel are provided with cybersecurity awareness and training so that they can perform their cybersecurity-related tasks"@en owl:sameAs "The organization’s personnel are provided with cybersecurity awareness and training so that they can perform their cybersecurity-related tasks"@en .

"The organization’s priorities, constraints, risk tolerance and appetite statements, and assumptions are established, communicated, and used to support operational risk decisions"@en owl:sameAs "The organization’s priorities, constraints, risk tolerance and appetite statements, and assumptions are established, communicated, and used to support operational risk decisions"@en .

"The organization’s technology assets are protected from environmental threats"@en owl:sameAs "The organization’s technology assets are protected from environmental threats"@en .

"The original NIST CSF 2.0 identifier (e.g. GV, GV.OC, GV.OC-01, GV.OC-01.Ex1). Retains period+dash convention from source; separate property alongside IRI conversion."@en owl:sameAs "The original NIST CSF 2.0 identifier (e.g. GV, GV.OC, GV.OC-01, GV.OC-01.Ex1). Retains period+dash convention from source; separate property alongside IRI conversion."@en .

"The overall management system, based on a business risk approach, to establish, implement, operate, monitor, review, maintain and improve information security. [ISO/IEC 27001:2022]"@en owl:sameAs "The overall management system, based on a business risk approach, to establish, implement, operate, monitor, review, maintain and improve information security. [ISO/IEC 27001:2022]"@en .

"The overall process of risk identification, risk analysis and risk evaluation. [ISO 31000:2018]"@en owl:sameAs "The overall process of risk identification, risk analysis and risk evaluation. [ISO 31000:2018]"@en .

"The overarching programme coordinating governance, risk management and compliance activities within the organisation."@en owl:sameAs "The overarching programme coordinating governance, risk management and compliance activities within the organisation."@en .

"The physical environment is monitored to find potentially adverse events"@en owl:sameAs "The physical environment is monitored to find potentially adverse events"@en .

"The recovery portion of the incident response plan is executed once initiated from the incident response processNIST CSWP 29 The NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF) 2.0"@en owl:sameAs "The recovery portion of the incident response plan is executed once initiated from the incident response processNIST CSWP 29 The NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF) 2.0"@en .

"The requirement is fully met with evidence."@en owl:sameAs "The requirement is fully met with evidence."@en .

"The requirement is met in part; gaps remain."@en owl:sameAs "The requirement is met in part; gaps remain."@en .

"The requirement is not met."@en owl:sameAs "The requirement is not met."@en .

"The risk owner is accountable for managing the risk."@en owl:sameAs "The risk owner is accountable for managing the risk."@en .

"The risk remaining after risk treatment has been applied."@en owl:sameAs "The risk remaining after risk treatment has been applied."@en .

"The risks posed by a supplier, their products and services, and other third parties are understood, recorded, prioritized, assessed, responded to, and monitored over the course of the relationship"@en owl:sameAs "The risks posed by a supplier, their products and services, and other third parties are understood, recorded, prioritized, assessed, responded to, and monitored over the course of the relationship"@en .

"The role is formally required by a legal instrument or standard."@en owl:sameAs "The role is formally required by a legal instrument or standard."@en .

"The role ultimately accountable for this obligation."@en owl:sameAs "The role ultimately accountable for this obligation."@en .

"The single top-level IB policy approved by senior management. [ISO 27001:2022 Cl.5.2 / ISO 27002:2022 §5.1]"@en owl:sameAs "The single top-level IB policy approved by senior management. [ISO 27001:2022 Cl.5.2 / ISO 27002:2022 §5.1]"@en .

"The thematic domain of the control in the SoA context (e.g. 'Organisatorisch', 'Technologisch')."@en owl:sameAs "The thematic domain of the control in the SoA context (e.g. 'Organisatorisch', 'Technologisch')."@en .

"The timing of control effect: Preventive, Detective, or Corrective."@en owl:sameAs "The timing of control effect: Preventive, Detective, or Corrective."@en .

"The top-level class for all governance, risk and compliance frameworks, regulations, standards, guidelines and best practices."@en owl:sameAs "The top-level class for all governance, risk and compliance frameworks, regulations, standards, guidelines and best practices."@en .

"The type of RACI assignment: Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, Informed."@en owl:sameAs "The type of RACI assignment: Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, Informed."@en .

"The ultimate obligation of a role for the outcome of a GRC activity. Only one actor may be accountable (A in RACI)."@en owl:sameAs "The ultimate obligation of a role for the outcome of a GRC activity. Only one actor may be accountable (A in RACI)."@en .

"The version string of the framework (e.g. '2022', 'Rev.5', 'v2.0')."@en owl:sameAs "The version string of the framework (e.g. '2022', 'Rev.5', 'v2.0')."@en .

"There is an awareness of cybersecurity risks at the organizational level, but an organization-wide approach to managing cybersecurity risks has not been established. Consideration of cybersecurity in organizational objectives and programs may occur at some but not all levels of the organization. Cyber risk assessment of organizational and external assets occurs but is not typically repeatable or reoccurring. Cybersecurity information is shared within the organization on an informal basis. The organization is aware of the cybersecurity risks associated with its suppliers and the products and services it acquires and uses, but it does not act consistently or formally in response to those risks."@en a xsd:string ;
    owl:sameAs "There is an awareness of cybersecurity risks at the organizational level, but an organization-wide approach to managing cybersecurity risks has not been established. Consideration of cybersecurity in organizational objectives and programs may occur at some but not all levels of the organization. Cyber risk assessment of organizational and external assets occurs but is not typically repeatable or reoccurring. Cybersecurity information is shared within the organization on an informal basis. The organization is aware of the cybersecurity risks associated with its suppliers and the products and services it acquires and uses, but it does not act consistently or formally in response to those risks."@en .

"There is an organization-wide approach to managing cybersecurity risks that uses risk-informed policies, processes, and procedures to address potential cybersecurity events. The relationship between cybersecurity risks and organizational objectives is clearly understood and considered when making decisions. Executives monitor cybersecurity risks in the same context as financial and other organizational risks. The organizational budget is based on an understanding of the current and predicted risk environment and risk tolerance. Business units implement executive vision and analyze system-level risks in the context of the organizational risk tolerances. Cybersecurity risk management is part of the organizational culture. It evolves from an awareness of previous activities and continuous awareness of activities on organizational systems and networks. The organization can quickly and efficiently account for changes to business/mission objectives in how risk is approached and communicated."@en a xsd:string ;
    owl:sameAs "There is an organization-wide approach to managing cybersecurity risks that uses risk-informed policies, processes, and procedures to address potential cybersecurity events. The relationship between cybersecurity risks and organizational objectives is clearly understood and considered when making decisions. Executives monitor cybersecurity risks in the same context as financial and other organizational risks. The organizational budget is based on an understanding of the current and predicted risk environment and risk tolerance. Business units implement executive vision and analyze system-level risks in the context of the organizational risk tolerances. Cybersecurity risk management is part of the organizational culture. It evolves from an awareness of previous activities and continuous awareness of activities on organizational systems and networks. The organization can quickly and efficiently account for changes to business/mission objectives in how risk is approached and communicated."@en .

"There is an organization-wide approach to managing cybersecurity risks. Cybersecurity information is routinely shared throughout the organization. Consistent methods are in place to respond effectively to changes in risk. Personnel possess the knowledge and skills to perform their appointed roles and responsibilities. The organization consistently and accurately monitors the cybersecurity risks of assets. Senior cybersecurity and non-cybersecurity executives communicate regularly regarding cybersecurity risks. Executives ensure that cybersecurity is considered through all lines of operation in the organization. The organization risk strategy is informed by the cybersecurity risks associated with its suppliers and the products and services it acquires and uses. Personnel formally act upon those risks through mechanisms such as written agreements to communicate baseline requirements, governance structures (e.g., risk councils), and policy implementation and monitoring. These actions are implemented consistently and as intended and are continuously monitored and reviewed."@en a xsd:string ;
    owl:sameAs "There is an organization-wide approach to managing cybersecurity risks. Cybersecurity information is routinely shared throughout the organization. Consistent methods are in place to respond effectively to changes in risk. Personnel possess the knowledge and skills to perform their appointed roles and responsibilities. The organization consistently and accurately monitors the cybersecurity risks of assets. Senior cybersecurity and non-cybersecurity executives communicate regularly regarding cybersecurity risks. Executives ensure that cybersecurity is considered through all lines of operation in the organization. The organization risk strategy is informed by the cybersecurity risks associated with its suppliers and the products and services it acquires and uses. Personnel formally act upon those risks through mechanisms such as written agreements to communicate baseline requirements, governance structures (e.g., risk councils), and policy implementation and monitoring. These actions are implemented consistently and as intended and are continuously monitored and reviewed."@en .

"There is limited awareness of cybersecurity risks at the organizational level. The organization implements cybersecurity risk management on an irregular, case-by-case basis. The organization may not have processes that enable cybersecurity information to be shared within the organization. The organization is generally unaware of the cybersecurity risks associated with its suppliers and the products and services it acquires and uses."@en a xsd:string ;
    owl:sameAs "There is limited awareness of cybersecurity risks at the organizational level. The organization implements cybersecurity risk management on an irregular, case-by-case basis. The organization may not have processes that enable cybersecurity information to be shared within the organization. The organization is generally unaware of the cybersecurity risks associated with its suppliers and the products and services it acquires and uses."@en .

